{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/75936-story-based-computer-games","id":75936,"title":"Story based computer games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-20T16:07:16-08:00","id":75936,"title":"Story based computer games","content":"Since the wod is very much story based, I think there are a lot of people here who like story based games. Which game do you like, because of it's story? I like most Telltale games (Walking Dead, Wolf Among Us) and I like Heavy Rain for example, although it had some plotholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T17:19:17-08:00","id":75973,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planescape:_Torment\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/06/Planescape-torment-box.jpg/256px-Planescape-torment-box.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Best game I ever read!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T18:26:03-08:00","id":76011,"title":"","content":"&quot;NWN2: Mask of the Betrayer&quot; and KOTOR 2 are two of my favorite games of all time because of their stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T18:37:49-08:00","id":76019,"title":"","content":"Arcanum of Steamworks and Magic Obscura actually impressed me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T22:53:45-08:00","id":76109,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I would second Planescape Torment. Fantastic storyline. KotOR 2 had a really deep story and, IMO, the best video game villain of all time. Unfortunately there were a few issues with the way the story came together due to the fact that the studio, Obsidian, had to rush the game out the door before it was totally finished.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T12:48:17-08:00","id":76503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/75936-story-based-computer-games?p=76109#post76109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I would second Planescape Torment. Fantastic storyline. KotOR 2 had a really deep story and, IMO, the best video game villain of all time. Unfortunately there were a few issues with the way the story came together due to the fact that the studio, Obsidian, had to rush the game out the door before it was totally finished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two of the best villains. The human void and the guy who should really be dead. Forgot their names and too lazy to search for them. I liked the story of the first kotor better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:11:34-08:00","id":76621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jan Paparazzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/75936-story-based-computer-games?p=76503#post76503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two of the best villains. The human void and the guy who should really be dead. Forgot their names and too lazy to search for them. I liked the story of the first kotor better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Anubis was referring to the game's final villain, Darth Traya. Darth Sion and Darth Nihilus were scary-powerful, and their utter reliance on the Force served to underscore the central thesis of KOTOR 2, but they were pretty much par for the course as Sith Lords - psycho dudes with unheard-of powers, being as evil as possible to everyone around them. (Although as a sidenote, Sion gets some depth with a female Exile, simultaneously loving the Exile for what she represents and hating himself for doing so.)<br /> <br /> Darth Traya is on an entirely different level, though. She's incredibly atypical for a Sith Lord - a weary old woman who hates the Force and wants to end its power over the galaxy. She balances being a caring maternal figure with being a misotheistic witch - subtle and manipulative when she needs to be, but stronger than anyone would imagine. And to a great degree, her philosophy - the thematic core of the game - is right.<br /> <br /> Basically, she's very different from most video game villains, and especially different from most Star Wars villains. It makes her stand out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T22:40:45-08:00","id":76877,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Darth Traya is one of the very few villains in a video game who had an ideology and goal that I absolutely found myself agreeing with, even as I found myself opposing her actions. Further, she is probably one of the most complex characters I've seen in a video game, or indeed, in any media. Her relationship with the Exile is equally complicated, and is really what brings the entire story together.<br /> <br /> She is essentially a heroic Paradise Lost-style Lucifer figure, only with the twist being that <i>God</i> is evil and must be overthrown. Even if she is crazy (or is she? her philosophy is hard to argue with, even if out-of-character we know that it's not something George Lucas ever intended) she's still very much a tragic heroine. She knows she can never succeed on her goal; she knows the only thing she can do is die, and yet she throws her life away in order to spit in the eye of fate; she sacrifices herself even as she understands that her sacrifice is totally and absolutely meaningless in the face of a malignant and invincible god. Her passion for saving the galaxy is equaled only against her love for the Exile (or at least what the Exile represents). Her love for the galaxy, love for the Exile and hatred of the Force are all teeteringly balanced against one another throughout the game and form her heroic/tragic character arc.<br /> <br /> I wish other games had characters and villains with that level of complexity to them, but it's really difficult to write something like that and make it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-22-2014, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T06:37:57-08:00","id":77627,"title":"","content":"So three of the best villains. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I really liked the premise of kotor 2, but in the end I found the story going down a little during the game. Kotor 1 was getting better during the game with a peak climax I can't tell, because of spoilers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T12:31:33-08:00","id":78503,"title":"","content":"I like games that have story, but sadly I very rarely play games because of them. Too often they are B movie or worse. They often read better than they actually play out. As to the question KOtOR 1, VtMR, and VtMB. I was liking The Void but like many one I set it down it wasn't enough for me to come back and finish the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T17:15:12-08:00","id":79775,"title":"",